# Standardized ART framework script. Frame is fixed; test logic is filled per step.
#
# ==== OBJECTIVE — expected results this script must demonstrate ====
#   - An ICMP Echo Reply returned for each unicast Echo Request addressed to the device,
#   with identifier, sequence number and payload unchanged.
#   - The Echo Reply source address identical to the destination address of the
#   corresponding Echo Request, on every interface that holds an address.
#   - On an interface with multiple addresses, each reply sourced from the specific address
#   that the matching request was sent to.
#   - Replies sourced from the requested address even when the reply leaves through a
#   different interface from the one owning that address.
#   - The Echo Reply source address following the requested address in a virtualised
#   management-fabric node as on a physical device.
#   - No Echo Reply sent for a request addressed to an address the device does not own, and
#   no reply sourced from an unrelated local address.
#   - Correct reply source selection maintained across address changes, with replies sourced
#   only from addresses currently configured.
